From c6b6dfc289e25ebc5810bdfb87659606481137e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:49:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/35] nx2: passthrough backend: 8192-entry GPFIFO rings,
 cached guest memory switch, GPU time profiler

- GPFIFO rings of 8192 entries (was 1024): with hardware acquires the front runs ahead, and a frame is ~8k guest
  entries; with 1024 it spun on a full ring (reading the fence over the BAR), unable to parse the channel the
  blocked one waited for. MKW racing ~17 -> ~21 fps.
- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SYSMEM_CACHED=1: guest system memory (and VT copies) GPU-cacheable, as on the console; the
  guest's own L2_SYSMEM_INVALIDATE / L2_FLUSH_DIRTY (~8 a frame) keep it coherent. PCIe reads 2-5.7 -> 1.3-3 GB/s.
- Acquires the backend inserts yield the GPU (ACQUIRE_SWITCH_TSG).
- Measuring: EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_GPUTIME=1 (GPU time per channel and per program, WFI timestamps around every
  submission), EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_WHERE=1 (where each colour target lives).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
